6:Real 3D support is not one feature, it is a **delivery problem first**. Only games where the server pushes (or Workshop auto-delivers) assets to players fit a hosting business. Hytale is the standout (new, server-first, open-ish formats). Rust, Fallout, GTA single-player and Valheim are poor fits. Build the foundation as **texture-first, PBR-channel-aware, delivery-aware**; do not build a mesh editor or text-to-3D now.
12:| **Hytale** | `.blockymodel` + PNG + JSON, asset pack = zip/folder with `manifest.json`; Blockbench (GPL-3, V api) + official plugin; no Windows-only tool (V: blog.curseforge.com/hytale-asset-editor-guide/, hytalemodding.dev/en/docs/guides/plugin/creating-block) | **Server streams to client at join, nothing installed by players** (V: curseforge blog; handshake detail U via host wikis) | Yes (server software availability on Linux U) | Server Operator Policies v1.1 cover monetisation/cosmetics/gambling, silent on mod ownership and AI (V: hytale.com/server-policies); EULA governs (U not read) | High: blocky low-res UV, PNG-only, same shape as our Minecraft bbmodel/RigSpec work | S-M | **START** |
